{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-17234-r4615206","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Coconut Chutney (South Indian)","sourcePageId":17234,"sourceRevision":"4615206","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:38:51Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Coconut%20Chutney%20(South%20Indian)&oldid=4615206","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:38:21.252Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Dal recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for chutney","Category:Recipes for curry","Category:Recipes using asafoetida","Category:Recipes using chickpea flour","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using cilantro","Category:Recipes using coconut","Category:Recipes using curry leaf","Category:Recipes using ginger paste","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Vegan recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"ace59916dfc8d69f8b644179565c41be2760b61bd0c3aa251260b19da20bc9c0","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Chutney recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Cuisine of India]] | [[Cookbook:Side dishes|Side Dishes]]\n\n'''Coconut Chutney''' is served as a [[Cookbook:Side dishes|side dish]] for a lot of [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Indian]] snacks and [[Cookbook:Breakfast Recipes|breakfast]] items. It can be mild to extra hot depending on the individual preference. This recipe is from South India.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== Base ===\n*1½ [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|Tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Chickpea|channa]] [[Cookbook:Dal|dal]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] finely-grated fresh [[Cookbook:Coconut|coconut]]\n*6–8 green hot [[Cookbook:Chiles|chile peppers]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Tamarind|tamarind]] paste\n*1 Tbsp [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Cilantro|cilantro]]\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]] paste\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n\n=== Seasoning ===\n*½ tsp [[Cookbook:Oil|oil]]\n*½ tsp [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard seed]]\n*3-4 [[Cookbook:Curry Leaf|curry leaves]], chopped\n*¼ tsp [[Cookbook:Asafoetida|asafoetida]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Dry [[Cookbook:Roasting|roast]] the channa dal until browned. Allow it to cool.\n# Grind the roasated dal, coconut, chiles, tamarind paste, cilantro, ginger paste, and salt in a [[Cookbook:Blender|blender]] with as little water as possible. For best results the final consistency must be somewhere between a coarse and smooth paste.\n# For seasoning, heat the oil in a small [[Cookbook:Ladle|ladle]]. Add the mustard seeds to hot oil, and allow them to crackle. When the crackling starts subsiding, add the asafoetida and the curry leaves, and stir for a few seconds.\n# Add the seasoning mixture to the chutney, and mix well.\n\n==See also==\n*[[Cookbook:Coconut Chutney (North Indian)|Coconut Chutney (North Indian)]]\n\n[[Category:Recipes for curry|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coconut]]\n[[Category:Indian recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Vegan recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes for chutney|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using asafoetida]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chickpea flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cilantro]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry leaf]]\n[[Category:Dal recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ginger paste]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Coconut Chutney (South Indian)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1½ Tbsp channa dal","sourceText":"1½ Tbsp channa dal","amountText":"1½ Tbsp channa dal","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 cup finely-grated fresh coconut","sourceText":"1 cup finely-grated fresh coconut","amountText":"1 cup finely-grated fresh coconut","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"6–8 green hot chile peppers","sourceText":"6–8 green hot chile peppers","amountText":"6–8 green hot chile peppers","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ tsp tamarind paste","sourceText":"½ tsp tamarind paste","amountText":"½ tsp tamarind paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 Tbsp chopped cilantro","sourceText":"1 Tbsp chopped cilantro","amountText":"1 Tbsp chopped cilantro","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 tsp ginger paste","sourceText":"1 tsp ginger paste","amountText":"1 tsp ginger paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"Salt to taste","sourceText":"Salt to taste","amountText":"Salt to taste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"½ tsp oil","sourceText":"½ tsp oil","amountText":"½ tsp oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"½ tsp mustard seed","sourceText":"½ tsp mustard seed","amountText":"½ tsp mustard seed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"3-4 curry leaves, chopped","sourceText":"3-4 curry leaves, chopped","amountText":"3-4 curry leaves, chop